From 85e7e297d56bd90fd3131250de27453dcbeff872 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:46:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Asynchronous computations on batches

Each batch function (integration, initialize functions, post-processings,
rotations, evaluation of the material properties) also takes an
asynchronous execution policy. It returns once the computations are
submitted, with a pending computation (PendingBatchComputation,
PendingBatchEvaluation) which holds the memory written or read by the
device and gives the result of the synchronous function once the calling
code has synchronized the queue. The status of the computations is
allocated by the memory resource of the policy, in memory accessible by
the host and by the computations. The synchronous functions are unchanged
and remain the default. Material properties: the report function and the
number of statuses of the generic-parallel interface are loaded.
