-The computations performed by `MGIS` are synchronous: the functions return
-once the computations are completed.
+With this policy, the computations are synchronous: the functions return
+once the computations are completed. This is the default: the functions
+without execution policy are synchronous.
+
+## Asynchronous computations
+
+Each batch function also exists with an asynchronous execution policy
+(`mgis::AsynchronousBatchExecutionPolicy`). The function then returns once
+the computations are submitted to the queue. The calling code can submit
+other computations, for instance the batches of other materials, and
+synchronize the queue once.
+
+~~~~{.cxx}
+auto p = AsynchronousBatchExecutionPolicy{};
+p.queue = stream;
+p.resource = &resource;  // managed memory
+p.location = MemoryLocation::SHARED;
+const auto pending = integrate(p, m, opts, dt);
+// ... other computations submitted to the stream
+cudaStreamSynchronize(stream);
+const auto r = pending.getResult();
+~~~~
+
+The asynchronous policy has the members of the synchronous one, plus:
+
+- `resource`: memory resource allocating the status of the computations,
+  or null for the memory of the host;
+- `location`: location of the memory allocated by this resource.
+
+The status of the computations is initialized and read by the host, and
+written by the device: it must be accessible by both. The memory of the
+host suits the backends computing on the host. Shared memory, allocated by
+a memory resource, suits all the backends.
+
+The functions return a pending computation:
+
+- `PendingBatchComputation` for the behaviours and the models
+  (integration, initialize functions, post-processings, rotations);
+- `PendingBatchEvaluation` for the material properties.
+
+Once the queue is synchronized, its `getResult` method gives the result
+returned by the synchronous function. The outputs must not be read
+before. The pending computation holds the memory written or read by the
+device: the status of the computations and, for the rotations, the
+rotation matrices built from material axes. It must not be destroyed
+before the computations are completed.
+
+`MGIS` can't synchronize the queue itself, since it does not depend on any
+GPU toolkit. The backends `stlpar` and `openmp` compute synchronously even
+with this policy, as `sycl` when data are transferred. With `sycl`, the
+queue must be in-order.
 
